# README gap 3 -- FIXED 2026-08-27 by the aggregation and projection
# family.
#
# `invoice.total = sum(lines[].amountCents)` was the single most natural
# invariant in this domain and it was inexpressible: there was no
# sum/fold/reduce, and `length()` could COUNT members but nothing could
# ADD them, so the model's totals were self-declared and spot-checked
# with per-record must() (seed.aon). A model asserting what it should be
# able to COMPUTE.
#
# It takes BOTH halves of the fix. `sum(d)` folds a bag with `add`, so
# the number tower's law comes with it -- these are integer cents and
# the total is an exact integer. But `sum` needs a bag of NUMBERS and a
# model holds a bag of RECORDS, so `pick(d, k)` is what gets from one to
# the other. `least` and `greatest` land with them.
# run: aontu gaps/agg-sum.aon
# expected: {"amounts":[3998,10],"largest":3998,"lines":[...],"total":4008}
# actual:   {"amounts":[3998,10],"largest":3998,"lines":[...],"total":4008}
lines: [ { amountCents: 3998 }, { amountCents: 10 } ]
amounts: pick($.lines, amountCents)
total: sum($.amounts)
largest: greatest($.amounts)
